{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Of Shaul, the family of…</b> Our Sages of blessed memory (Numbers Rabbah 21:3) said, and this is their language: Rabbi Yochanan said, five names were called upon him: Zimri, etc., Shaul son of the Canaanitess, etc. And it is difficult according to the words of the midrash — since the Shaul mentioned here is Zimri, why does HaShem trace his name to the family named after him? For did they not say of blessed memory (Yoma 38a) regarding the verse ״וְשֵׁם רְשָׁעִים יִרְקָב״ that we do not conclude with their names — how much the more so to seal with his name, blessed be He! And according to one of the approaches we explained on the verse (Numbers 25:14) ״אֲשֶׁר הֻכָּה אֶת הַמִּדְיָנִית״ — that he was struck only while she was with him and not afterward — this is what HaShem justified in His utterance here, that He sealed his name upon it. And this is also implied by their words of blessed memory (Numbers Rabbah 21:3), for they said, and this is their language: Shaul — שֶׁהִשְׁאִיל עַצְמוֹ לַעֲבֵרָה, and the law of a loan that returns to its owner is well known."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:14:42.932631890Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}